1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:11,880
Do you ever wake up with a fuzzy feeling in your head, you can't concentrate on anything, or find your memory just isn't working as it should?
你是否曾在醒来时感到头脑昏沉，无法集中注意力，或者发现记忆力不如往常？

2
00:00:11,880 --> 00:00:13,170
You're not alone.
你并不孤单。

3
00:00:13,170 --> 00:00:21,220
39% of British people said they suffer brain fog on a regular basis in a FutureYou Cambridge study.
FutureYou剑桥研究显示，39%的英国人表示他们经常遭受脑雾的困扰。

4
00:00:21,220 --> 00:00:25,480
But why do we get brain fog, and can we do anything to prevent it?
但我们为什么会出现脑雾，我们能做些什么来预防它呢？

5
00:00:25,480 --> 00:00:30,120
The technical word for brain fog is cognitive impairment.
脑雾的专业术语是认知障碍。

6
00:00:30,120 --> 00:00:37,580
When you have it, you can't think as clearly as you normally can – just as if your brain was actually full of fog.
当你有脑雾时，你无法像往常那样清晰地思考——就好像你的大脑真的充满了雾。

7
00:00:37,580 --> 00:00:53,040
Dr Brennan, a neuroscientist and author, says "Brain fog is different to these short-term disruptions, because it is persistent, occurs regularly and can interfere with the quality of your life, your relationships, and your work".
神经科学家兼作家布伦南博士说："脑雾与这些短期干扰不同，因为它是持续性的，经常发生，并且会干扰你的生活质量、人际关系和工作。"

8
00:00:53,040 --> 00:01:03,570
The reality is that no-one knows exactly what causes it, though theories include chemical or blood flow changes in the brain, and low-level inflammation.
事实是，没有人确切知道是什么导致了脑雾，尽管有一些理论涉及大脑中的化学或血流变化，以及低度炎症。

9
00:01:03,570 --> 00:01:07,080
What we do know are factors that make it worse.
我们所知道的是那些会使情况恶化的因素。

10
00:01:07,080 --> 00:01:13,940
Fatigue, for example, is a key contributor to brain fog, making it hard to stay focused.
例如，疲劳是导致脑雾的一个关键因素，使人难以保持专注。

11
00:01:13,940 --> 00:01:23,170
This is because sleep deficiency can change activity in some parts of the brain, which means processing and recalling detail becomes harder.
这是因为睡眠不足可以改变大脑某些部分的活动，这意味着处理和回忆细节变得更加困难。

12
00:01:23,170 --> 00:01:31,210
Pain and anxiety can also contribute to it – they interfere with cognitive speed because they are distracting.
疼痛和焦虑也可能导致脑雾——它们会干扰认知速度，因为它们会分散注意力。

13
00:01:31,210 --> 00:01:39,270
There are also medical conditions that can make it worse, like long Covid or autoimmune conditions like lupus disease.
还有一些医疗状况会使情况恶化，比如长新冠（新冠后遗症）或狼疮等自身免疫性疾病。

14
00:01:39,270 --> 00:01:44,170
So, if you're suffering from brain fog, what can you do to fix it?
那么，如果你正遭受脑雾的困扰，你能做些什么来解决它呢？

15
00:01:44,170 --> 00:01:49,490
One thing you can do is avoid ultra-processed foods (UPFs).
你可以做的一件事是避免超加工食品。

16
00:01:49,490 --> 00:02:07,140
Dr Megan Rossi, the founder of The Gut Health Doctor, told the BBC that "UPFs are often low in essential nutrients like magnesium, omega-3 fatty acids and iron, all of which are crucial for brain function and mental clarity".
肠道健康医生创始人梅根·罗西博士告诉BBC："超加工食品通常缺乏镁、欧米伽-3脂肪酸和铁等必需营养素，而所有这些都对大脑功能和思维清晰至关重要。"

17
00:02:07,140 --> 00:02:15,200
Therefore, we should pack our diets with nutrient-rich foods like whole grains, vegetables and healthy fats.
因此，我们应该在饮食中多摄入营养丰富的食物，如全谷物、蔬菜和健康脂肪。

18
00:02:15,200 --> 00:02:23,770
Blueberries are particularly rich in polyphenols and have been shown to improve cognitive function and memory in clinical trials.
蓝莓尤其富含多酚，在临床试验中已被证明可以改善认知功能和记忆力。

19
00:02:23,770 --> 00:02:26,710
Hydration is also very important.
补水也非常重要。

20
00:02:26,710 --> 00:02:33,460
So, if you feel a bit foggy, try to get more sleep and consider making some changes to your diet.
所以，如果你感觉有点昏沉，试着多睡一会儿，并考虑改变一下你的饮食。
